.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_MAC-POLY1305 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_MAC-Poly1305
.Nd The Poly1305 EVP_MAC implementation
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Support for computing Poly1305 MACs through the
.Sy EVP_MAC
API.
.Ss Identity
This implementation is identified with this name and properties, to be
used with
.Xr EVP_MAC_fetch 3 :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqPOLY1305", \(dqprovider=default"
.El
.Ss Supported parameters
The general description of these parameters can be found in
.Xr EVP_MAC 3 .
.Pp
The following parameter can be set with
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_set_params 3 :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqkey" ( Ns Sy OSSL_MAC_PARAM_KEY Ns ) <octet string>
Sets the MAC key.
Setting this parameter is identical to passing a
.Em key
to
.Xr EVP_MAC_init 3 .
.El
.Pp
The following parameters can be retrieved with
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_get_params 3 :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqsize" ( Ns Sy OSSL_MAC_PARAM_SIZE Ns ) <unsigned integer>
Gets the MAC size.
.El
.Pp
The "size" parameter can also be retrieved with with
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_get_mac_size 3 .
The length of the "size" parameter should not exceed that of an
.Sy unsigned int .
.Sh NOTES
The OpenSSL implementation of the Poly 1305 MAC corresponds to RFC 7539.
.Pp
It is critical to never reuse the key.
The security implication noted in RFC 8439 applies equally to the
OpenSSL implementation.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_get_params 3 ,
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_set_params 3 ,
.Xr EVP_MAC 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
